  "question": {
    "text": "In an ac circuit, an inductor, a capacitor and a resistor are connected in series with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Impedance of this circuit is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Zero",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Recall the formula of impedance&nbsp;is in terms of resistance,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math>, here, the condition of resonance,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></math>, it means,&nbsp;<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi></math>"
  }
}